{
 "esm": "1.2.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "makearray_nested_reduction_dynamic",
  "description": "A `makearray` whose region value is an array `faq` with a rank-0 `faq` reduction nested in its body (the EarthSciASTDiff contracted-band shape, issue #547): one region; `[0, nested]` over the same box with the loop indices read as numbers; overlapping regions where the last wins, with an inner window and a rank-0 total; a gap left at the 0 default; a fold whose terms are all -0.0; and a two-dimensional makearray with a rank-1 face value and a rank-2 value. The data alternate 1e16 magnitudes, so any fold other than the per-cell build's left-to-right one disagrees by whole units. Dynamic variant: the same rules beside states whose right-hand sides are such makearrays, one of them reading a state in the nested sum, so the nested reduction runs on every call.",
  "authors": [
   "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
  ],
  "tags": [
   "native",
   "conformance"
  ]
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "x": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": 9
  },
  "rows": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": 2
  }
 },
